# Binary artifacts this repository deliberately tracks.
#
# Read by `scripts/check_binary_artifacts.py` (bead
# enhancedchannelmanager-6mqn5). That guard fails a pull request which ADDS a
# credential-bearing or bulk binary artifact. This file is its escape hatch.
#
# FORMAT: one exact repository-relative path per line, followed by a `#` and a
# reason. The reason is mandatory and the guard rejects an entry without one:
# it is the review artifact, and an entry nobody had to justify is
# indistinguishable from turning the guard off for that file.
#
#     e2e/fixtures/sample-upload.zip  # 40-byte fixture, no credentials, bd-xxxxx
#
# Globs are rejected. `*.zip` would re-open the hole this guard closes in a
# single line; the value of the hatch is that a human named one file and said
# what it was.
#
# BEFORE ADDING AN ENTRY, check that the artifact is not simply a drill
# leftover. Playwright's upload sandbox forces artifacts into the repository
# root during backup/restore drills, and the correct disposition for those is
# deletion, not an allowlist entry.
#
# This file is empty on purpose. The repository tracks no archive, no
# database, and no binary outside the image types the guard already accepts;
# `backend/tests/unit/test_check_binary_artifacts.py` asserts that against the
# live tracked tree, so an entry here would be a real exception rather than
# routine bookkeeping.
